6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Only rebar.audit.server._audited_tickets consumes store_uninitialized; it degrades to an empty index for that code and propagates all others. No caller depends on the old []-for-broken-store.'","server.py:101 branches `if rebar.error_code_for(exc) != \"store_uninitialized\": raise` then returns an empty index for that code","server.py docstring (:94): 'every OTHER failure still propagates, so a genuinely broken store is not silently blanked' — a promise the widened code breaks","Existing test test_audit_index_still_propagates_a_non_store_read_failure pins that only non-`store_uninitialized` failures propagate; a broken store now returns `store_uninitialized`, so the audit index blanks it and the test does NOT catch this because it injects `command_failed`, not a real broken-store read"],"finding":"Widening `store_uninitialized` to fire for broken/mid-clone stores collides with the audit-server consumer, which degrades that exact code to an empty page — silently blanking a genuinely broken store, the same masking this change exists to remove.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f29a9a94f8078cbd2","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan -> 'Caller-dependency gate (verified)'; interacts with src/rebar/audit/server.py:101 and tests/unit/test_reads_uninitialized_store.py:163","norm_id":"n07dc452af7457c24","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["MCP/audit web index pointed at a store mid-clone or with no .git renders an empty page instead of signalling the store is broken","The production scenario in section 1 (marker files, no .git) would now render as an empty audit index rather than surfacing the fault"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Either (a) keep `store_uninitialized` only for ABSENT/no-.git and introduce a separate code (e.g. `store_unusable`) for mid-clone/broken so the audit degrade stays scoped to truly-uninitialized, or (b) explicitly state and test that the audit index SHOULD blank broken/mid-clone stores too, updating the server.py docstring's 'genuinely broken store is not silently blanked' promise and extending the propagate-test to cover a real broken-store read.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how store_is_usable classifies non-HEAD git subprocess failures (git-missing / timeout / unexpected non-zero): define whether these raise a distinct error vs mapping to store_uninitialized, and instrument the failure path (log/metric) so an environmental failure is distinguishable from a genuine mid-clone.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.615,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'git via `git -C tracker`' and 'HEAD resolves' — the plan defines the success path but not the failure taxonomy of the subprocess call","This adds a new external/subprocess failure point (git invocation) whose non-HEAD-related failures are not classified"],"finding":"The new predicate shells out to `git -C tracker rev-parse --verify -q HEAD` but the plan does not specify how store_is_usable handles subprocess failures that are NOT 'HEAD unresolvable' — e.g. git binary missing, subprocess timeout, permission error, or a corrupt-repo non-zero exit for an unrelated reason. Any such transient/environmental failure would be silently collapsed into store_uninitialized, indistinguishable from a legitimately mid-clone store.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f88f6b716c7d934f2","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan -> Design: store_is_usable(tracker); AC 'mid-clone (.git present, HEAD unresolvable)'","norm_id":"n0e98cbf97dbf65e7","priority":0.335,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["git not on PATH in a stripped deploy image -> every read reports store_uninitialized","transient FS/permission hiccup during rev-parse -> a healthy store momentarily reads as uninitialized"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"State that only a clean 'HEAD unresolvable' (rev-parse exits non-zero with empty output) maps to store_uninitialized, while git-not-found / timeout / other errors surface as a distinct diagnostic error, and add a log line on that branch. Add a predicate test asserting the distinction.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Have `store_is_usable` compose the existing `gitutil._resolve_tracker_git_dir` (worktree/gitdir-pointer-safe, 7+ call sites, stdlib-only at module scope) for the '.git present' half and `gitutil.run_git` for the HEAD probe, rather than re-deriving `.git` detection in the new leaf.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: \"New stdlib-only leaf ... store_is_usable(tracker) = isdir AND .git present AND HEAD resolves (git via git -C tracker; .git-exists check precedes the HEAD probe ...)\"","gitutil.py:72 `def _resolve_tracker_git_dir(tracker)` handles `.git`-as-file (gitdir: pointer) AND `.git`-as-dir, returning '' when absent — the exact '.git present' predicate, worktree-safe","gitutil.py module-level imports are stdlib + only `from rebar._store import git_outcome` (git_outcome is stdlib-only), so it is importable without the write-core SCC the plan cites as the reason for a separate module","grep: `_resolve_tracker_git_dir` has >=7 non-test consumers (fsck.py, fsck_scan.py, fsck_repair.py, bridge_repair.py, fsck_recover.py, tracker_maintenance.py, gitutil internals)","event_prepare._ensure_initialized (line 101) currently uses naive `os.path.exists(os.path.join(tracker, '.git'))`, which the plan folds into the shared predicate — an opportunity to adopt the worktree-correct primitive rather than perpetuate the naive check"],"finding":"The new leaf `store_usability.store_is_usable` re-derives the '`.git` present' check instead of composing the existing shared stdlib-only primitive `gitutil._resolve_tracker_git_dir`, which already answers that question, is already used by 7+ call sites, and already handles the `.git`-as-file gitdir-pointer / linked-worktree form that a naive `.git`-exists probe misses.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ffacc633710a4828e","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan -> Design / Files (`src/rebar/_store/store_usability.py` new; predicate '`.git` present AND HEAD resolves')","norm_id":"ncb04f9906f05bad3","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A tracker attached as a linked git worktree (`.git` is a `gitdir:` FILE, not a dir): a naive `.git`-present check in the new leaf may misjudge usability where `_resolve_tracker_git_dir` would resolve it correctly","Future divergence: the new leaf's `.git` detection drifts from the 7 existing call sites' shared detection, re-introducing the multiple-private-checks class the codebase already consolidated"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Define `store_is_usable(tracker)` as: `os.path.isdir(tracker) and bool(gitutil._resolve_tracker_git_dir(tracker)) and gitutil.run_git(tracker, 'rev-parse', '--verify', '-q', 'HEAD', check=False).returncode == 0`. Keeping the new leaf module (for the import-SCC boundary the plan cites) is fine — just import and reuse the existing stdlib-only gitutil primitives instead of re-implementing `.git`-presence detection.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_i